## 1. Scope

This reference covers heavy wall heat shrink sleeving for 26/35 kV busbars. At this class the wall is thick enough that recovery uniformity around the bar becomes the practical issue, not the dielectric property of the compound.

## 2. Construction

- Heavy wall cross-linked polyolefin based sleeving with anti-tracking fillers.
- Thick wall retains heat during recovery, so cooling has to be controlled rather than accelerated.
- Supplied in large diameters for step and flat bar profiles.
- Available with adhesive lined ends where the termination of the sleeve has to be sealed.

